  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The flow – shot, wall pass and diagonal",
  "description": "One line in each corner at one end and a cone on each side further out. A runs round the cone, gets a diagonal pass from line D and shoots first time. At the same time B starts their run on the other side. After the shot A turns back towards their own corner, gets the ball from C and plays it straight back. C then plays a first-time diagonal pass to B, who has rounded their cone and shoots first time. B then turns towards line D for their extra pass, and so it keeps going.\n\nRotation: after your wall pass, join the other line. Keep the tempo high so it flows. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stay alert right after the shot – the next job is waiting."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Passes should be flat and without bounce."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Play the diagonal pass early, in front of the runner."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "warmup",
  "focus": [
    "passing",
    "shooting"
